          "id": "60e3f84c1e9ef2dc6a9352a131e825d3e60894c1",
          "message": "perf(engine): use contiguous bind-join groups for sorted inputs (#4350)\n\n* feat: resolve target issue #3190 [opus5]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: address review round 1 for #4350 [opus5]\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* perf(engine): reuse presorted bind-join groups\n\nKeep the existing hash grouping for unsorted input; use contiguous borrowed\nruns when sorted_by matches the join key. Share the scan, filter, budget and\ntrace body through a monomorphic owned/borrowed slice adapter.\n\nRetain randomized multiset differential coverage for both strategies and\ndeclare the measured intentional default-WASM change without changing floors.\nFull engine library suite: 314 passed, 2 ignored. All-target clippy passes.\nDisabling the presorted fast path makes its focused test fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: OpenAI GPT-6 Astra <noreply@openai.com>\n\n* fix(engine): verify bind-join sortedness before grouping\n\nCheck nondecreasing join Ids before trusting sorted_by for run grouping;\nstale metadata retains hash grouping with one bound scan per distinct key.\nPreserve the output metadata and existing scan/filter/budget/zk body.\n\nExercise real SELECT reachability, budget failure, randomized stale input,\nand behavioral mutation controls. Record final-source native A/B evidence\nlocally and refresh the intentional feature-OFF WASM declaration without\nchanging the size floor.\n\nCo-Authored-By: OpenAI GPT-6 Astra <noreply@openai.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: sparq-orchestrator[bot] <305236749+sparq-orchestrator[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <63333554+jeswr@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: OpenAI GPT-6 Astra <noreply@openai.com>",
